    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Backup n8n workflows to individual JSON\nCreate by [Eddy Balaya](https://linktr.ee/eddybalaya)\n## How to use\n**1. Setup n8n API**\nGo to setting > n8n API > Create API\nCreate Credential: \n- Copy API Key\n- Copy https://yourdomain.com/api/v1; replace \"your domain with your n8n host URL\n\n**2. Setup Gdrive Credential**\n- Create a folder (to store your backups)\n- Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/ > APIs & Services\n- Click on \"+ Enable APIs and services\" \n- Search for \"Drive\", select \"Google Drive API\" exactly (not the other ones)\n- Click on OAuth Consent Screen > Data Access > Add or remove scope\n- Search for \"drive\" or \"drive.file\" in \"Enter property name or value\"\n    - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive (full Drive access)\n    - OR https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file (only files created by the app — more restrictive)\n- Click on \"Update\"\n- Click on Clients > + Create client > Web application\n- Name your app (ex \"n8n-gdrive\")\n- in n8n, in \"Upload to Google Drive\" node, Create new credential or edit existing one\n- copy \"OAuth Redirect URL\"\n- Go back to Google Cloud Console, Click \"+Add URI\" and copy URL copied above\n- Click Create\n- Final step, in \"APIs & Services\" > \"Audience\", add User (yourself, a personal email that you use to connect to Gdrive. \n\n- Execute workflow and enjoy!\n\n\n[Leave a 5 star review, if it was worth it!](https://share.google/5K3liTiDiZ6waXDKW)",
        "height": 720,
        "width": 880
      },
